{"kind":"request","text":"Serve dap cards from the hosted MCP endpoint\n\nScope: matrix task 3, with task 10 for the remote card origin, from\nreport cb825288 and order 58c6cb8e. The matrix is\n~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-02-mcp-host-requirements-audit/matrix.md,\nwith corrections.md beside it. Claude and ChatGPT come first.\n\nToday packages/mcp/src/hosted.ts builds each hosted agent's\nMcpService with no view source, so a host that reaches /mcp gets\ntools but no cards. The stdio service in packages/mcp/src/node.ts\nserves cards from a declared view source.\n\nThe scene: an agent enrolled on a hosted Worker serves its room\nthrough /mcp. A UI-capable host lists the same card tools and\nresources that the stdio service lists for that room, reads a card\nresource, and a card press makes the same signed act as on stdio.\n\nThe work:\n\n1. Give HostedAgent the view source of its room's installed\n   application, so that the hosted card list equals the stdio list\n   for a capable host. A host that does not declare the UI capability\n   gets no card metadata, as on stdio.\n2. Let a deployment declare a full card origin per host for remote\n   resources: {hash}.claudemcpcontent.com for Claude, from the SHA-256\n   of the configured URL, and a unique origin for ChatGPT. Never\n   declare one on stdio.\n3. Keep authority unchanged. Every card act is signed by the hosted\n   agent's own key and judged by its scope.\n\nDone when a scripted UI-capable host, through the hosted /mcp route of\na local Worker build, lists and reads the cards and makes one press to\nits act, with a test, a control for a host that does not declare UI,\nand the checker's review. Hosted MCP stays closed on the deployed\nWorkers. The live Claude and ChatGPT runs come after OAuth.\n\nOrder: after G3 source child d5cc652b reaches review, ahead of Goose\nrequest d23fb0b6.","body":{"conditions":"A scripted UI-capable host lists, reads and presses dap cards through the hosted /mcp route of a local Worker build, a host without UI gets no card metadata, per-host remote card origins are declared, authority is unchanged, the checker reviews, and the head lands on main.","target_head":"04f4af480be161c94f3df745747ab7fd68755314","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}